                                <DTC ID="DTCB206B4B" OID="50a04b1e-688d-4c03-9647-dbed92c47fdb">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB206B4B</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10513227</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B206B4B</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_864720427">Over temperature - Temperature Driver too high</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_712048008">no service</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1154175090">1. Check if external lamps are working 
2. Check wireharness of external lamps
3. If 1. and 2. are OK check external lamp outputs (trigger light output)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1282258365">Ignition ON</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1620650512">Continous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_603488216">100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1670425825">NTC temperature above threshold</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_2014819334">NTC temperature below threshold</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_341741195">1. Deactivation of external lamps</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1777454293">1. If first failure criteria occurs the aging counter is set to 40
2. If error-free detection cycle without a "test failed" in previous and current driving cycle, aging counter is decremented by 1 
3. If aged counter reaches 0, the DTC Aged Criteria is fufilled</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1731597348">1. Current for the external lights too high
2. Short circuit in wireharness of external lamps
3. Short circuit in external lamp.
4. External lamp outputs of OHC defective.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
